\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf {The reconstructed encoding circuit for $G^\top $'s column-linear entries.} A ripple-carry adder shifts the $n$-qubit column-index register into the form the ladder consumes, and is uncomputed afterwards. A ladder of $n$ singly-controlled $R_y(\theta _m)$ rotations accumulates the amplitude $\mathrm {raw}(p)$ of \Cref {eq:app-ladder-raw} on one flag qubit by exact angle addition; a second, independently controlled ladder applies the row-zero correction. Ancilla: $n+4$ total (\Cref {app:pihm-circuit}).}}{9}{figure.caption.20}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Measured subnormalisation and spectral-gap collapse of the composed $H$, $n=2$ to $8$.} (a) $\alpha _H$ against $N=2^n$ on log-log axes, empirically $\Theta (N^8)$, against $\|H\|=\Theta (N^2)$. (b) Relative spectral gap of the composed $H$ against $n$, falling to $\sim 10^{-15}$ by $n\gtrsim 7$, below double-precision machine epsilon (dashed line).}}{10}{figure.caption.21}%
